---
description: Keep Flutter widgets focused, decomposed, and files within size limits
alwaysApply: true
---

# Widget Structure & File Size

## No Business Logic in UI Files

Widgets are for layout and presentation only. Any logic that fetches data, transforms state, or makes decisions belongs in a provider/notifier — never inline in a widget:

```dart
// ❌ BAD — business logic in a widget
class OrderScreen extends ConsumerWidget {
  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context, WidgetRef ref) {
    final orders = ref.watch(ordersProvider);
    final filtered = orders.where((o) => o.status == 'active').toList()
      ..sort((a, b) => b.createdAt.compareTo(a.createdAt));
    return ListView(children: filtered.map((o) => OrderTile(o)).toList());
  }
}

// ✅ GOOD — logic lives in the notifier, widget just renders
// In orders_notifier.dart:
List<Order> get activeOrders => state.where((o) => o.status == 'active').toList()
  ..sort((a, b) => b.createdAt.compareTo(a.createdAt));

// In order_screen.dart:
class OrderScreen extends ConsumerWidget {
  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context, WidgetRef ref) {
    final orders = ref.watch(ordersNotifierProvider.notifier).activeOrders;
    return ListView(children: orders.map((o) => OrderTile(o)).toList());
  }
}
```

## One Widget Per File

Each file should contain one primary public widget. Small, tightly-coupled private helper widgets (`_MyHelper`) can live in the same file, but extract them once they grow beyond ~50 lines.

## File Line Limit: 300 Lines

No Dart file should exceed 300 lines. If it does:
- Split large screens into smaller sub-widgets
- Move logic into a provider/notifier
- Extract reusable widgets into a shared `widgets/` folder

## Extract Widgets as Classes, NOT Methods

Helper methods (`_buildHeader()`) are a Flutter anti-pattern — they re-run on every rebuild and lose `const` optimisation:

```dart
// ❌ BAD
Widget _buildAvatar() => CircleAvatar(...);

// ✅ GOOD
class _Avatar extends StatelessWidget {
  const _Avatar();
  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) => const CircleAvatar(...);
}
```

## Extract Inline Callbacks

Avoid fat anonymous lambdas in widget trees. Extract them to named methods for readability and testability:

```dart
// ❌ BAD
ElevatedButton(
  onPressed: () {
    final result = doSomething();
    if (result) navigate();
    else showError();
  },
  child: const Text(AppStrings.submit),
)

// ✅ GOOD
ElevatedButton(onPressed: _handleSubmit, child: const Text(AppStrings.submit))

void _handleSubmit() {
  final result = doSomething();
  if (result) navigate();
  else showError();
}
```

## Keep `build()` Shallow

`build` should read like a table of contents. If it exceeds ~40 lines or 4–5 levels of nesting, decompose into sub-widgets.

## Prefer `SizedBox` over `Container` for Spacing

```dart
// ❌ BAD
Container(height: 16)

// ✅ GOOD
const SizedBox(height: 16)
```
